 "notes": "ROUGH: digitized from a watermarked web image for use as a search seed, not a benchmark.\nSource: Clash Champs base #101332 (https://www.clashchamps.com/i-need-a-base/?search_player_townhalls=16&order_by=1), builder \"Reyferro\", uploaded 2026-08-27, Clash Champs tag \"Pro\" (386 downloads on 2026-10-21). Image: https://clashchamps.com/cdn-cgi/imagedelivery/m4td0QhRkBTnwv62pP40vA/94d93a04-2abc-4d56-5b10-8140fdabdc00/image1920 (1318x927 village screenshot, green scenery with lake, Clash Champs watermark over the centre). Layout link: https://link.clashofclans.com/en/?action=OpenLayout&id=TH16%3AHV%3AAAAAFQAAAALIhJEW8ep9gZuuokZ2xa9F .\nDigitized 2026-10-21. Grid: cx 651.8, top 64.87, a 10.952, b 8.214 (screen = cx + (x-y)a, top + (x+y)b). Scale and slope from a comb fit of the wall-cap lines (ratio 0.750, line period 2b = 16.43 px) confirmed by the FFT of the checkered grass (period 21.9 x 16.4 px); sub-tile phase from the checkered grass pattern (correlation 5.2 vs 0.001 at the worst phase; phase step 0.05 tile; grid lines visually on the checker edges). Integer anchoring: the checker region spans exactly x 0..43 / y 0..43 and the outermost buildings touch both opposite edges (camp at 0,0; camp at 0,40; hero hall at 40,0). Note: decorations (cakes, Christmas trees) stand outside the 44x44 grid on the border, which the game allows; they are ignored.\nResolution is low (tile half-width 11 px). Building identities were matched against TH16-era sprite references (chiefpansancolt/clash-of-clans-data images). Positions were read from the bottom tip of each sprite's base (+-1 tile). The base is MERGED (2 Ricochet Cannons, 2 Multi-Archer Towers, 3 Cannons, 4 Archer Towers).\nUncertain identities: dsf (green cauldron), barracks (purple/red building with waterfall at 0,27), dbarracks (dark/red machine), helper (orange round hut), lab (bronze machine) - army/utility buildings only; 2 scatter (washed-out teal sprites under the watermark), 1 sweeper (tall brown sprite under the watermark), 1 banner (purple flag). Seasonal Crafting Station present as Cake-A-Pult (pink cake on a grey platform), mode cake. Modes assumed: infernos single (single flame seen), x-bows both, spell towers rage (purple orbs), sweepers face the centre.\nOverlaps resolved by 1-tile nudges: at 7,5->7,6 (to fit dsf), dd 2,33->3,34, dd 3,36->3,37, banner 20,6->20,7, dbarracks 36,0->37,0, helper 41,3->41,4, mat 36,11->36,10, tesla 38,24 (from 38,25), gs 41,29->41,30, ec 41,9->41,10, mortar 41,34->41,33; smith clamped from x=-1 to 0, hero hall placed at 40,0 (bottom-tip read gave y=-1).\nIMPUTED (1): B.O.B's Hut not identified -> placed at bob 15,0 (nearest free spot to the workshop corner).\nWalls: automatic cap detection (steel highlight + gold cap colour masks, sampled 9.2 px above tile centres) minus building footprints, runs of 2+ kept; the watermark and tall buildings hide some walls, so the count is below 325. Traps are visible in the screenshot (giant-bomb pairs, spring traps, air-bomb cluster near the centre, seeking mines/skeleton traps) but were NOT transcribed. Levels not set.\nSEED COMPLETION (tools/baselab/digitize_kit/seed.py, rng seed 16, from reyferro-cc101332.json): walls 231 -> 325: 94 walls ADDED by baselab.generator.top_up_walls (dead-end spikes/single posts next to existing walls, not the builder's design): 0,17 0,22 0,24 1,17 1,18 1,22 1,24 1,26 2,17 2,18 2,22 2,24 2,26 4,18 4,19 4,20 8,13 8,14 8,15 8,16 10,18 10,19 14,18 14,19 14,25 15,18 15,19 15,25 15,29 15,30 15,31 16,25 16,28 17,17 17,25 17,28 18,17 19,11 19,12 19,13 19,17 19,24 20,2 20,3 20,12 20,13 20,24 21,24 21,42 22,42 23,37 23,38 23,42 23,43 24,15 24,16 24,19 24,24 24,42 24,43 25,19 25,24 25,40 26,15 26,16 26,17 26,19 26,24 26,26 26,40 27,26 28,38 29,27 29,32 29,33 29,34 29,38 29,40 29,41 29,42 30,27 31,18 31,19 32,27 32,28 33,29 33,30 34,20 34,27 34,28 35,20 37,17 37,18 37,19. Traps: 44 ADDED on free tiles inside the convex hull of the walls (wall ring has gaps), spread by farth